Z||000000||SloPonti||10-27-1999||11:17 PM||||I was wondering if any of your fieros feature alarms(after market of course) and has anyone of you fieros been broken into or vandilized? I currently have a viper with remote start and keyless entry and like it very well! Does anyone else have an alarm?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||10-27-1999||11:41 PM||||Just before college started up for this semester I had a Viper alarm installed in my Formula.  Had the siren mounted under the drivers side headlight, just next to the radiator, in a little cavity(very loud).  Impossible to find, even the alarm guys couldn't find it after I relocated it.(from inside the front compartment!!!)  Very sweet little setup. Never had any problems with the alarm or break-ins.  At the old apartment, quite a few cars were "hit", mine was never touched.  Doesn't mean it will never happen.  I feel it just gives one more little piece of protection.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||10-28-1999||12:01 AM||||I dont have an alarm in my car. But when I go to Wal Mart or the mall (both prime places for break ins in my area) I just take my Australian Shephard with me. She is the absolute ugliest dog anybody has ever seen and they think it is some kind of wolf dog. No break-ins yet, just a little blue dog hair in the passenger seat.||||reg||14
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||10-28-1999||12:52 AM||||I had an 84 Trans Am while living in Houston Tx. One morning I came outside to see my wheels (aftermarket sawblade) and Yokohama tires were gone and the car was on blocks. Then in 94 I had a lifted 91 S10 with Lacara steering wheel and Centerline Convo Pro wheels and a serious sound system. One morning I came outside to find the stereo and amps gone and a window busted out. Then a month later they came back and took the whole truck! Most of it was found but it was totalled. I now have a Code Alarm in my 94 S10 that has remote locks. I used to have the same alarm in my 86 SE but took it out when I got rid of it. I kinda liked it in my 86 because of the remote trunk release and plan to install it in my 88.||||reg||8
Z||000004||Bugsy||10-28-1999||08:15 AM||||I have an auto page brand alarm with a 4 watt transmitter that pages me when the alarm is tripped. Its supposed to have a 3 mile radius but i haven't tested it. I had it installed due to hits in my  complex lot and my work lot...mine hasn't been hit yet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||10-28-1999||09:15 AM||||I had a Serpico alarm system installed on my last car ('88 Dodge Shadow) when it was new...voltage sensor type that goes off when anything is opened...also had a motion sensor/glass breakage sensor.<P>Liked it so well I took it off the Shadow and put it on the Fiero...very easy install (one wire) and the remotes have a much longer range through the plastic.<P>I don't know if Serpico is around any more, but the voltage sensor alarms are an easy install and a lot cheaper than they used to be. Just bought one for my wife's car for less than $30.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||10-28-1999||11:10 AM||||i had a one in my 86 GT, with a interior motion sensor.  after i first installed it, whenever i would stay at my then girlfriends, cats would stay undernieth the car and set the alarm off.  one nite @ 2 am, the alarm sounded, i checked and reset it, 10 min later it went off and i did the same, 10 min later it went off again.  thinking i had a short, i  turned it off (my EX girlfriend was also screaming at me about it.  when i went to my car in the morning the sunroof was laying in front of the car (they popped the latch) and my casett case and $100 cig lighter was gone!  they baited me!  but that is the only time i have ever been broken into!  to bad they didn't steal the girlfriend...that would of saved me a lot of trouble  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !!||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Fiero||10-28-1999||11:44 AM||||On my '88 Fiero I have the Mongoose alarm...it has dual stage sensor,controls the trunk and door locks, the windows are included in which If I want ventilation I just push a button and it drops about 1/2 inch down and also if I left my windows down, it will roll up automatically. My ignition kill is not hook on the ignition as like other alarm installation. It is hook up the computer brain, that way total control of it. If something goes wrong with the alarm there is a by-pass connector that you can use to avoid a total dead ECM...<P>I used to have a '85 Mazda RX-7 and I have a special alarm in that car. I always leave my Python inside and one night someone tries to get in by breaking the glass sunroof...but when he met "Ed" he was screaming at the top of his voice..woke up the whole neighborhood... The police came and an ambulance...the guy had to be carried in a strecther..."Ed" is almost 9 feet long and have him for a long time... He is lucky I fed him that night...he he he ||||reg||1
